WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:08.540
Speaker 1: So the next piece of this seven
hours of missing call logs story is the obviously

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:14.259
unbelievable claim from Donald Trump that
he doesn't even know what burner phones are.

00:00:14.259 --> 00:00:20.020
So as a reminder, yesterday we reported to
you White House records turned over to the

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:25.470
January six committee are missing about seven
and a half hours of logs.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.759
This is a key seven and a half hours.

00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:34.940
While the insurrection was going on, and one
of the sort of notable things that came out

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:40.480
of this was that Donald Trump denied having
any idea what a burner phone is.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:45.440
In a statement Monday night, Trump said, I
have no idea what a burner phone is.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.850
To the best of my knowledge, I have never
even heard the term.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.810
This stunk to high heaven.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:56.400
And when I told you this yesterday, the story
we didn't know about John Bolton's recent

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.311
comments, it was not plausible that Trump
didn't know the term burner phone, and it

00:01:02.311 --> 00:01:08.220
was certainly not plausible that Trump doesn't
know about disposable phones.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:13.141
If you wanted to be as charitable as possible
and give Trump the benefit of the doubt, which

00:01:13.141 --> 00:01:16.470
I don't know why we would do at this point,
but let's say we did.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:21.750
You might be able to argue Trump knows of
them as disposable phones, and he doesn't

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.420
know or remember the term burner phone, but
that wasn't even believable.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:26.590
It really wasn't.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:31.780
We now have new reporting from Donald Trump's
former national security adviser, who says

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.920
he specifically remembers Trump using the
term burner phones.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.840
And of course, this is completely believable
and completely obvious, and it's what we suspected

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:40.920
right away.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:46.030
CBS News reporting John Bolton, the former
national security adviser to Trump, told CBS

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:51.119
News he heard Trump use the phrase burner
phones in several discussions and that Trump

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:54.439
did know exactly what it meant.

00:01:54.439 --> 00:01:57.860
In a response, Trump said he never heard the
phrase burner phone.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:01.450
I have no idea what a burner phone is to the
best of my knowledge, I've never even heard

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:02.970
the term.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:07.070
Bolton says he and Trump spoke about how people
have used burner phones to avoid having their

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:08.320
calls scrutinized.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:14.739
I mean, you know, I know Trump's not the brightest.

00:02:14.739 --> 00:02:19.239
But it did not pass the sniff test that Trump
didn't know what a burner phone was.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.549
And this is increasingly reeking of Watergate.

00:02:21.549 --> 00:02:26.189
I would encourage everybody in the audience
who is disturbed by this story, as you should

00:02:26.189 --> 00:02:28.469
be, and you want to read a little bit more
about it.

00:02:28.469 --> 00:02:33.579
There's a really good new piece in the New
Republic by Alex Shepard called Trump's missing

00:02:33.579 --> 00:02:39.319
phone records have a familiar think of criminality.

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:47.450
And in that article, Alex Shepherd discusses
the analogies here to Watergate and mentions

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:54.780
that in terms of the amount of missing phone
data, it is more than 20 times longer in terms

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.749
of a gap in the records than what there was
in the Watergate tapes.

00:02:58.749 --> 00:03:03.519
I don't know how many have recently reviewed
Watergate in all of its different elements,

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:09.010
but one of the things about Watergate was
a gap in tapes which ultimately scandalized

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:13.779
Richard Nixon and led to his resignation in
1974.

00:03:13.779 --> 00:03:18.620
And the gap in the record with these Trump
phone calls is more than 20 times bigger than

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:22.180
the gap in that in the Watergate tapes.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:26.709
The difference, of course, is that at the
time, Richard Nixon was president, and so

00:03:26.709 --> 00:03:29.889
the entire scandal precipitated his resignation.

00:03:29.889 --> 00:03:31.060
Trump is no longer president.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:35.219
And of course, you and I would like to think
if people are reasonable, Republicans would

00:03:35.219 --> 00:03:39.209
say, OK, even if I liked his tax plan, this
is just too much.

00:03:39.209 --> 00:03:42.680
I can't vote for the guy in 2024.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.099
Unfortunately, that's not the case.

00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:49.439
And not only are there tens of millions of
voters at least still willing to vote for

00:03:49.439 --> 00:03:55.010
Donald Trump still eager to vote for Donald
Trump in 2024, they become more emboldened

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.010
by these stories.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:04:02.200
If you go and you look at right wing, YouTube,
right wing Twitter right wing talk shows like

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:06.939
Real America's Voice and Newsmax and all all
these different places, you see that they

00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:11.999
are actually emboldened by these stories,
saying these are part of the witch hunt attacks

00:04:11.999 --> 00:04:14.829
meant to take down Trump unfairly.

00:04:14.829 --> 00:04:20.810
We renew our support for him as a result of
this investigation, which is really scary

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:21.810
stuff.

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:25.760
We'll have all these articles and more on
our Instagram.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.880
You can follow us there, The David Pakman
Show.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.260
We'll take a break.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:31.620
We will talk about that.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.090
Rick Scott 11.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.600
Wacky plan.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.330
After this short break

